e gallery epic (launch verified with a tutorial packaged in the format), not as a DAG edge — the gallery can be developed and reviewed against a draft tutorial while the curated set is authored. |\n| E003 ∥ E004 | Rule 1 / Rule 14 | Different components and teams (Notebooks/Workbenches vs Data Science Pipelines/RHOAI Pipelines); no shared artifacts beyond the common format both already depend on. |\n| E001, E002, E003, E004 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs last) | The documentation describes the gallery, the tutorial set, and the contribution process as built, so it is blocked by every Implementation epic in the strategy. |\n\n## HLR Traceability Matrix\n\n| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) | Notes |\n|-----|----------|---------|-------|\n| HLR-1 (tutorial gallery with one-click launch) | P0 | E002 | Direct mapping. |\n| HLR-2 (six curated, tested tutorials) | P0 | E003, E004 | Split along the component/team boundary: five notebook-based journeys (first workbench, data prep, first training run, first deployment, first RAG app) in E003; the pipeline-based journey (first pipeline) in E004. Both cover HLR-2 together; neither alone satisfies it. |\n| HLR-3 (tutorial packaging format) | P1 | E001 | Epic raised to P0 by priority inheritance: the format gates all P0 delivery (HLR-1 and HLR-2 both build against it), so the prerequisite inherits the highest priority it transitively enables. See Health Warnings. |\n| HLR-4 (gallery and contribution documentation) | P2 | E005 | `docs-authoring` priority exception: derived from strategy frontmatter `priority: Major` → P1. |\n\nAll four HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n\n## Health Warnings\n\n- **Missing strategy sections (non-blocking):** the strategy has no Impacted Teams\n  table, no Dependencies table, no formal Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, and\n  no non-functional requirements section. Teams were inferred from the\n  architecture-context owning teams (Dashboard → RHOAI Dashboard, Notebooks →\n  Workbenches, Data Science Pipelines → RHOAI Pipelines; the Documentation team\n  has no context file and was assigned by convention). Acceptance criteria below\n  were derived from the HLRs.\n- **Priority inheritance, not inversion:** HLR-3 is labeled P1, but its epic (E001)\n  is P0 because every P0 deliverable (gallery and tutorials) builds against the\n  format. This is standard prerequisite priority inheritance, flagged here for\n  reviewer visibility.\n- **Scope trap — RAG journey (architecture claim uncorroborated):** HLR-2 includes\n  a \"first RAG app\" tutorial, but no architecture-context file covers a RAG\n  capability in the platform (no context file exists for Llama Stack or any other\n  RAG-bearing component). The tutorial epic is unaffected — it is authored either\n  way — but if no supported RAG surface exists at release time, that one tutorial\n  may need to build the RAG app from generic workbench/serving primitives or be\n  descoped. Verify during epic refinement; this does not change the epic DAG.\n- **Component mapping note (E001):** the packaging format is consumed by the\n  Dashboard gallery implementation and by both tutorial-content epics, so its work\n  spans several strategy components. It is assigned the single canonical component\n  `Dashboard` as the most-relevant consumer (the gallery parses the metadata and\n  launch mechanics use the pinned images), owned by RHOAI Dashboard.\n- **Tutorial-type assumption:** the strategy does not state which of the six\n  tutorials are notebooks and which are pipelines. This decomposition assumes five\n  notebook-based and one pipeline-based tutorial. If refinement assigns more\n  journeys to pipelines, move them into the pipeline tutorial epic — a content\n  reassignment within the same DAG, no structural change.\n\nNo epic exceeds the ~2-week epic-size guideline; the six tutorials are split\nacross two teams and the gallery is one Dashboard feature.\n\n## Tiered Delivery\n\nNot applicable. The strategy has no external dependencies with uncertain timing\n(no upstream contributions, vendor coordination, or third-party gating); all work\nis in-platform and ships together.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":33028,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9126a4174cb3c3e5","agent_id":"a81bb8d060212c78b","session_id":"7d9fc257-6641-4b77-aebe-6dc2ab6f744b","uuid":"cb5caea9-81c3-497d-8f89-a700fb232fe8","timestamp":"2026-10-25T19:07:41.282Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9019 into epics"}
