{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-abb65dd89a371b72","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9019\n3\tepic_count: 5\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\trevised: false\n7\ttriage: null\n8\ttriage_rationale: null\n9\t---\n10\t# RHAISTRAT-9019 Decomposition — Curated getting-started tutorial gallery\n11\t\n12\tStrategy: RHAISTRAT-9019 (Curated getting-started tutorial gallery, priority Major,\n13\tstatus Refinement Done).\n14\t\n15\tTriage: full decomposition. The strategy is not below threshold — its problem\n16\tstatement explicitly identifies three architecturally distinct work streams with\n17\tdifferent owners and review processes (product code for the gallery and launch\n18\tmechanics, substantive content authoring of the tutorials themselves, and\n19\tdocumentation), spanning multiple components and teams. It is not documentation-only.\n20\t\n21\tAll components referenced by the strategy (Dashboard, Notebooks, Data Science\n22\tPipelines) have architecture-context files in `.context/architecture-context/`\n23\t(rhoai-3.0), so no onboarding chains or provisioning investigations are required.\n24\tNotebooks and Data Science Pipelines are **passive** components in this strategy:\n25\tthe launch mechanics use their existing, documented interfaces (Notebook CRD via\n26\tthe Dashboard; KFP v2 pipeline import), so no code changes are needed in them.\n27\tTheir validation is folded in as acceptance criteria on the gallery launch epic\n28\tand the tutorial testing epics; because the validating teams (Workbenches, RHOAI\n29\tPipelines) own the tutorial content epics that exercise those paths, no separate\n30\tvalidation epics are generated.\n31\t\n32\t## Epic List\n33\t\n34\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n35\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n36\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E001 | Tutorial packaging format and validation manifest | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P0 |\n37\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E002 | Dashboard tutorial gallery with one-click launch | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P0 |\n38\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E003 | Curated notebook tutorials for core getting-started journeys | Implementation | Workbenches | P0 |\n39\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E004 | First-pipeline tutorial | Implementation | RHOAI Pipelines | P0 |\n40\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E005 | Gallery usage and tutorial contribution documentation | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Documentation | P1 |\n41\t\n42\t## Dependency DAG\n43\t\n44\t```mermaid\n45\tgraph TD\n46\t    E001[\"E001 Tutorial packaging format\"] --> E002[\"E002 Dashboard tutorial gallery\"]\n47\t    E001[\"E001 Tutorial packaging format\"] --> E003[\"E003 Notebook tutorials\"]\n48\t    E001[\"E001 Tutorial packaging format\"] --> E004[\"E004 First-pipeline tutorial\"]\n49\t    E002[\"E002 Dashboard tutorial gallery\"] --> E005[\"E005 Gallery documentation\"]\n50\t    E003[\"E003 Notebook tutorials\"] --> E005[\"E005 Gallery documentation\"]\n51\t    E004[\"E004 First-pipeline tutorial\"] --> E005[\"E005 Gallery documentation\"]\n52\t```\n53\t\n54\tCritical path length: 3 (E001 → any of E002/E003/E004 → E005).\n55\t\n56\t## DAG Justification\n57\t\n58\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n59\t|------|------|-----------|\n60\t| E001 → E002 | Rule 13 (build-against artifact) | The gallery's listing and launch mechanics build against the tutorial packaging format (its metadata model and pinned-image scheme) — the Dashboard code consumes the format as an API-like artifact, so the format must exist first. |\n61\t| E001 → E003 | Rule 13 (build-against artifact) | Notebook tutorials are packaged and validated per the format (metadata, pinned images, validation manifest); authoring against an unsettled format would double-touch every tutorial. |\n62\t| E001 → E004 | Rule 13 (build-against artifact) | The pipeline tutorial is packaged and validated per the same format. |\n63\t| E002 ∥ E003, E002 ∥ E004 | Rule 14 (different repos, no shared artifacts) | Gallery code and tutorial content live in different repos owned by different teams. The end-to-end coupling is expressed as an AC on the gallery epic (launch verified with a tutorial packaged in the format), not as a DAG edge — the gallery can be developed and reviewed against a draft tutorial while the curated set is authored. |\n64\t| E003 ∥ E004 | Rule 1 / Rule 14 | Different components and teams (Notebooks/Workbenches vs Data Science Pipelines/RHOAI Pipelines); no shared artifacts beyond the common format both already depend on. |\n65\t| E001, E002, E003, E004 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs last) | The documentation describes the gallery, the tutorial set, and the contribution process as built, so it is blocked by every Implementation epic in the strategy. |\n66\t\n67\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n68\t\n69\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) | Notes |\n70\t|-----|----------|---------|-------|\n71\t| HLR-1 (tutorial gallery with one-click launch) | P0 | E002 | Direct mapping. |\n72\t| HLR-2 (six curated, tested tutorials) | P0 | E003, E004 | Split along the component/team boundary: five notebook-based journeys (first workbench, data prep, first training run, first deployment, first RAG app) in E003; the pipeline-based journey (first pipeline) in E004. Both cover HLR-2 together; neither alone satisfies it. |\n73\t| HLR-3 (tutorial packaging format) | P1 | E001 | Epic raised to P0 by priority inheritance: the format gates all P0 delivery (HLR-1 and HLR-2 both build against it), so the prerequisite inherits the highest priority it transitively enables. See Health Warnings. |\n74\t| HLR-4 (gallery and contribution documentation) | P2 | E005 | `docs-authoring` priority exception: derived from strategy frontmatter `priority: Major` → P1. |\n75\t\n76\tAll four HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n77\t\n78\t## Health Warnings\n79\t\n80\t- **Missing strategy sections (non-blocking):** the strategy has no Impacted Teams\n81\t  table, no Dependencies table, no formal Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, and\n82\t  no non-functional requirements section. Teams were inferred from the\n83\t  architecture-context owning teams (Dashboard → RHOAI Dashboard, Notebooks →\n84\t  Workbenches, Data Science Pipelines → RHOAI Pipelines; the Documentation team\n85\t  has no context file and was assigned by convention). Acceptance criteria below\n86\t  were derived from the HLRs.\n87\t- **Priority inheritance, not inversion:** HLR-3 is labeled P1, but its epic (E001)\n88\t  is P0 because every P0 deliverable (gallery and tutorials) builds against the\n89\t  format. This is standard prerequisite priority inheritance, flagged here for\n90\t  reviewer visibility.\n91\t- **Scope trap — RAG journey (architecture claim uncorroborated):** HLR-2 includes\n92\t  a \"first RAG app\" tutorial, but no architecture-context file covers a RAG\n93\t  capability in the platform (no context file exists for Llama Stack or any other\n94\t  RAG-bearing component). The tutorial epic is unaffected — it is authored either\n95\t  way — but if no supported RAG surface exists at release time, that one tutorial\n96\t  may need to build the RAG app from generic workbench/serving primitives or be\n97\t  descoped. Verify during epic refinement; this does not change the epic DAG.\n98\t- **Component mapping note (E001):** the packaging format is consumed by the\n99\t  Dashboard gallery implementation and by both tutorial-content epics, so its work\n100\t  spans several strategy components. It is assigned the single canonical component\n101\t  `Dashboard` as the most-relevant consumer (the gallery parses the metadata and\n102\t  launch mechanics use the pinned images), owned by RHOAI Dashboard.\n103\t- **Tutorial-type assumption:** the strategy does not state which of the six\n104\t  tutorials are notebooks and which are pipelines. This decomposition assumes five\n105\t  notebook-based and one pipeline-based tutorial. If refinement assigns more\n106\t  journeys to pipelines, move them into the pipeline tutorial epic — a content\n107\t  reassignment within the same DAG, no structural change.\n108\t\n109\tNo epic exceeds the ~2-week epic-size guideline; the six tutorials are split\n110\tacross two teams and the gallery is one Dashboard feature.\n111\t\n112\t## Tiered Delivery\n113\t\n114\tNot applicable. The strategy has no external dependencies with uncertain timing\n115\t(no upstream contributions, vendor coordination, or third-party gating); all work\n116\tis in-platform and ships together.\n117\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aae824fdc3467597","agent_id":"ac4672d82971598e7","session_id":"7d9fc257-6641-4b77-aebe-6dc2ab6f744b","uuid":"6df4a8b0-8e8b-4a39-90cd-0f6b5f81b234","timestamp":"2026-10-25T19:10:42.369Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-abb65dd89a371b72","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9019 decomposition"}
