{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-adf645e9f16318e3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9019-E001\n3\ttitle: Tutorial packaging format and validation manifest\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9019\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 0\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: -1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 3\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Tutorial packaging format and validation manifest\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tDefines the packaging format that curated tutorials use so they are versioned and\n34\ttestable independently of Dashboard releases. The format covers the three elements\n35\tthe strategy names: tutorial metadata, pinned images, and a validation manifest.\n36\tIt is the shared artifact that both the Dashboard tutorial gallery (which lists\n37\ttutorials from their metadata and launches them using their pinned images) and the\n38\tauthored tutorial content (which is packaged and validated per the format) build\n39\tagainst.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Define the metadata that describes a packaged tutorial, sufficient for a gallery\n44\t  to list it and a consumer to understand what it covers.\n45\t- Define how tutorial images are pinned so that launching a tutorial is\n46\t  reproducible against a known target release.\n47\t- Define the validation manifest used to test a packaged tutorial, so each\n48\t  tutorial can be validated against the current release on its own cadence,\n49\t  independently of Dashboard release cycles.\n50\t- Define versioning rules for packaged tutorials.\n51\t- Publish the format specification where the Dashboard gallery implementers and\n52\t  the tutorial authoring teams can build against it.\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- The packaging format is documented and covers metadata, pinned images, and a\n57\t  validation manifest, as required by the strategy.\n58\t- A tutorial packaged in the format can be versioned and validated independently\n59\t  of a Dashboard release: running its validation manifest against a target\n60\t  release produces a deterministic pass/fail result.\n61\t- The format specification is reviewed and agreed by the teams that build against\n62\t  it — the Dashboard gallery implementers and the tutorial authoring teams —\n63\t  before dependent work consumes it.\n64\t- The format specification is committed to an accessible platform repository.\n65\t\n66\t## HLR Traceability\n67\t\n68\t- HLR-3 (P1 — tutorial packaging format). This epic is prioritized P0 by\n69\t  inheritance: the gallery and all curated tutorials build against the format,\n70\t  so it gates the strategy's P0 delivery.\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aae824fdc3467597","agent_id":"ac4672d82971598e7","session_id":"7d9fc257-6641-4b77-aebe-6dc2ab6f744b","uuid":"e2caa6ad-d7e8-4d8b-b695-58ea728c8406","timestamp":"2026-10-25T19:10:45.915Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-adf645e9f16318e3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9019 decomposition"}
