{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-acf156c4b27566ed","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-9019\n3\tscore: 14\n4\tpass: true\n5\trecommendation: accept\n6\tissues:\n7\t- severity: minor\n8\t  criterion: Epic Boundaries\n9\t  description: E003 bundles five curated, tested tutorials (authoring + packaging\n10\t    + release testing), placing it at the upper bound of the ~2-week guideline while\n11\t    the summary asserts no overage. Record the concrete re-split trigger in the Health\n12\t    Warnings (e.g. if authoring and validating the five tutorials outgrows a single\n13\t    sprint of effort, split the epic along journey lines, such as first-workbench/data-prep/first-training\n14\t    vs first-deployment/first-RAG-app) so the overage is a managed watch item rather\n15\t    than an unacknowledged risk.\n16\terror: null\n17\t---\n18\t## Review Summary\n19\t\n20\tScore: 14/14 — pass\n21\tRecommendation: accept\n22\t\n23\tContract validator: OK (`validate_decomposition.py RHAISTRAT-9019` exited 0 — epic body\n24\tsections, canonical component names, Rule 11 docs-last coverage, priority inheritance,\n25\timplementation-type parallelism, and epic-size triggers all pass). Triage consistency:\n26\t`triage` is null (full decomposition) with `epic_count: 5` — multi-epic output is\n27\texpected; no contradiction.\n28\t\n29\tThe decomposition cleanly separates the strategy's three work streams (product code,\n30\tcontent authoring, documentation) into distinct epics along component/team boundaries,\n31\tmaps all four HLRs with a traceability matrix, keeps E002/E003/E004 parallel with the\n32\tformat (E001) as the sole shared prerequisite, and places the docs-authoring epic (E005)\n33\tlast per Rule 11. Frontmatter `dependencies` match the summary DAG edge-for-edge, arrows\n34\tfollow the dependency→dependent convention, and the critical path (3) fits the strategy\n35\tsize. One minor watch item on E003 sizing.\n36\t\n37\t## Criterion Details\n38\t\n39\t### 1. HLR Coverage (2/2)\n40\tAll four HLRs map to at least one epic: HLR-1 → E002, HLR-2 → E003+E004 (split along\n41\tthe component/team boundary, both needed to satisfy it), HLR-3 → E001, HLR-4 → E005.\n42\tTraceability matrix is present. Priority inheritance is correct: E001 (HLR-3, labeled\n43\tP1) is raised to P0 because it blocks all P0 delivery — properly flagged in Health\n44\tWarnings. E005 is `docs-authoring` and exempt from priority inheritance; its P1 derives\n45\tcorrectly from the strategy's `priority: Major`. No priority collapse: no epic bundles\n46\tHLRs at multiple priority levels with deferrable lower-priority features (E001 carries\n47\tonly HLR-3; E002 only HLR-1; E003/E004 share HLR-2 at the same priority).\n48\t\n49\t### 2. DAG Coherence (2/2)\n50\tNo circular dependencies; all edges reference existing epics. Diagram↔frontmatter\n51\tcross-check: E002 deps [E001], E003 deps [E001], E004 deps [E001], E005 deps\n52\t[E001,E002,E003,E004] — exactly matches the six diagram edges, arrows drawn\n53\tdependency→dependent per convention. Every edge is justified in the DAG Justification\n54\ttable: E001→{E002,E003,E004} under Rule 13 (build-against artifact — the format is the\n55\tshared spec all three build against); E002∥E003∥E004 correctly left parallel (Rule 14,\n56\tdifferent repos/teams); the end-to-end gallery↔tutorial coupling is expressed as an AC\n57\tgate on E002 (\"launch verified with at least one tutorial packaged in the format\"), not\n58\ta DAG edge — the rule-compliant shape for content consumed at runtime. Rule 11:\n59\tE005 (docs-authoring) is blocked by all four Implementation epics. No\n60\tkonflux-onboarding/license-validation epics exist, so Rules 7/8/10 parallelism is not\n61\tapplicable. No conditional branch files. Critical path length 3 (E001 → any\n62\timplementation → E005) is appropriate for an M-size strategy. No data/artifact\n63\tdependency in epic content is missing from the DAG. Validator confirms all mechanical\n64\tchecks.\n65\t\n66\t### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n67\tEach epic has a distinct component/team tuple: E001/E002 Dashboard+RHOAI Dashboard,\n68\tE003 Notebooks+Workbenches, E004 Data Science Pipelines+RHOAI Pipelines, E005\n69\tDocumentation+RHOAI Documentation. Work-product types are properly separated — the\n70\tstrategy's three kinds of work (product code, content authoring, documentation) land in\n71\tseparate epics with no code/content mixing. E003 and E004 split HLR-2 along the\n72\tcomponent/team boundary, not duplicating any surface (different journeys, different\n73\tcomponents). E001's cross-component consumption is acknowledged and assigned a single\n74\tcanonical component (Dashboard) with rationale. One minor watch item: E003 bundles five\n75\tcurated, tested tutorials, which sits at the upper bound of the ~2-week guideline — see\n76\tissues (record a re-split trigger).\n77\t\n78\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n79\tAll five epics are Implementation and each produces a concrete artifact (format spec,\n80\tgallery feature, five tutorials, one tutorial, published documentation). No\n81\tInvestigation epics — correctly, since the strategy lists no open questions and no\n82\toutcome changes downstream epic structure. E001 is rightly Implementation (it delivers\n83\ta specification artifact; its outcome does not gate the existence of downstream epics).\n84\tNo `gated_by`/`gate_failure_impact` fields are set anywhere, and no epic depends on an\n85\tInvestigation, so no gating metadata issues apply.\n86\t\n87\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n88\tAll epics are Implementation and carry `ai_signals` (the 9-signal rubric);\n89\t`investigation_signals` is null throughout — type-appropriate. Frontmatter values match\n90\tthe ai-signals rationale files for all five epics. Spot checks: E001's\n91\t`human_process_gates: -1` is justified by its own cross-team sign-off AC; E002's\n92\t`pattern_precedent: 1` and `e