{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b56666e6751f23a3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-9019\n3\tscore: 12\n4\tpass: false\n5\trecommendation: revise\n6\tissues:\n7\t- severity: critical\n8\t  criterion: DAG Coherence\n9\t  description: 'E005 frontmatter lists RHAISTRAT-9019-E001 in dependencies and the\n10\t    DAG Justification table asserts E001, E002, E003, E004 -> E005 (Rule 11), but\n11\t    the mermaid DAG diagram omits the E001 --> E005 edge — frontmatter/diagram mismatch.\n12\t    Correction: add the E001 --> E005 edge to the mermaid diagram so it matches the\n13\t    frontmatter dependencies and the justification table.'\n14\terror: null\n15\t---\n16\t# Decomposition Review — RHAISTRAT-9019\n17\t\n18\t## Review Summary\n19\t\n20\tScore: 12/14 — fail\n21\tRecommendation: revise\n22\t\n23\tContract validator: OK (all mechanical checks passed: epic body sections,\n24\tcanonical component names, Rule 11 docs-last coverage, priority inheritance,\n25\timplementation-type parallelism, epic-size overage triggers).\n26\t\n27\tTriage consistency: `triage: null` (full decomposition) with 5 epics —\n28\tmulti-epic output is expected; no contradiction.\n29\t\n30\tOne critical issue found by the diagram/frontmatter cross-check (Criterion 2),\n31\twhich forces that criterion to 0 and triggers the auto-fail rule regardless of\n32\tthe total score.\n33\t\n34\t## Criterion Details\n35\t\n36\t### 1. HLR Coverage (2/2)\n37\tAll four HLRs map to epics: HLR-1 (P0) → E002; HLR-2 (P0) → E003 + E004\n38\t(five notebook journeys + one pipeline journey = six tutorials, split along the\n39\tcomponent/team boundary); HLR-3 (P1) → E001; HLR-4 (P2) → E005. The\n40\ttraceability matrix is present and complete. Priority inheritance is correct:\n41\tE001 is raised to P0 because it gates all P0 delivery — the prerequisite\n42\tinherits the priority of the work it enables, and this is flagged in Health\n43\tWarnings. E005 (docs-authoring, P1) is exempt from priority inheritance per the\n44\tdocs-authoring exception (strategy priority Major → P1) — not flagged. No\n45\tpriority collapse: each epic maps to HLRs at a single effective priority level;\n46\tE003's five journeys are all P0 HLR-2 content under one team, not deferrable\n47\tfeatures bundled with P0 work. No lower-priority epic blocks P0 work.\n48\t\n49\t### 2. DAG Coherence (0/2)\n50\tThe DAG structure itself is sound: no cycles; every frontmatter dependency\n51\treferences an existing epic; E002/E003/E004 run in parallel after E001\n52\t(Rule 14, different repos/teams, no shared artifacts — correct, not\n53\tover-serialized); the gallery↔tutorial coupling is correctly expressed as an\n54\tacceptance criterion on E002 rather than a DAG edge; critical path length 3 is\n55\tappropriate for the strategy size; no konflux-onboarding / license-validation /\n56\trepo-onboarding epics exist, so Rules 7/8/10 parallelism is not implicated; no\n57\tconditional branch files exist.\n58\t\n59\tHowever, the cross-check consistency requirement fails in one direction:\n60\tE005's frontmatter `dependencies` lists RHAISTRAT-9019-E001 (correct per Rule 11\n61\t— the docs-authoring epic must be blocked by every Implementation epic, and the\n62\tDAG Justification table explicitly asserts \"E001, E002, E003, E004 → E005\"),\n63\tbut the mermaid DAG diagram draws only `E002 --> E005`, `E003 --> E005`, and\n64\t`E004 --> E005` — the `E001 --> E005` edge is missing from the diagram. Every\n65\tfrontmatter dependency must have a matching edge in the summary diagram; this\n66\tmismatch makes the diagram inconsistent with the frontmatter (and with the\n67\tsummary's own justification table) and misleading about E005's blocking set,\n68\teven though the frontmatter is correct. Per the review rules this is a critical\n69\tissue and scores 0.\n70\t\n71\tCross-check completeness: no data/artifact dependency discoverable from epic\n72\tcontent is missing from the DAG — E002, E003, E004 all consume the packaging\n73\tformat and all edge to E001; the tutorial content E002 consumes for launch\n74\tverification is correctly an AC gate, not a DAG edge.\n75\t\n76\t### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n77\tEach epic has a single component/team tuple: E001/E002 (Dashboard / RHOAI\n78\tDashboard), E003 (Notebooks / Workbenches), E004 (Data Science Pipelines /\n79\tRHOAI Pipelines), E005 (Documentation / RHOAI Documentation). The\n80\twork-product-type separation is exactly what the strategy demands: product code\n81\t(E002), format specification (E001), tutorial content authoring (E003/E004),\n82\tand documentation (E005) are separate epics — no code-plus-content mixing. No\n83\tscope duplication: E003 and E004 author disjoint journey sets in different\n84\tcomponents; the overlapping references to the workbench/pipeline paths in E002\n85\tvs E003/E004 are validation coverage of passive components through different\n86\tsurfaces (launch mechanics vs tutorial journey), not rebuilt deliverables, and\n87\tthe decomposition explicitly documents this folding. E003 sits at the upper\n88\tbound of the ~2-week guideline but is one logical work stream (same team, same\n89\tformat, same testing pass) and carries a concrete, actionable re-split trigger\n90\tin Health Warnings (split along journey lines if effort outgrows a sprint) — a\n91\ttriggered, justified overage, so no deduction. E001's cross-component\n92\tconsumption is acknowledged with a single canonical component assignment.\n93\t\n94\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n95\tAll five epics are Implementation and each produces a concrete artifact (format\n96\tspecification, gallery feature, tutorial sets, documentation). No Investigation\n97\tepics exist, which is correct: the strategy lists no open questions and no\n98\tcomponent lacks architecture context, so there is no uncertainty that changes\n99\tdownstream structure. All `gated_by`/`gate_failure_impact` fields are null and\n100\tno