{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-87931a482bffa201","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9019\n3\tepic_count: 5\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\trevised: true\n9\t---\n10\t# RHAISTRAT-9019 Decomposition — Curated getting-started tutorial gallery\n11\t\n12\tStrategy: RHAISTRAT-9019 (Curated getting-started tutorial gallery, priority Major,\n13\tstatus Refinement Done).\n14\t\n15\tTriage: full decomposition. The strategy is not below threshold — its problem\n16\tstatement explicitly identifies three architecturally distinct work streams with\n17\tdifferent owners and review processes (product code for the gallery and launch\n18\tmechanics, substantive content authoring of the tutorials themselves, and\n19\tdocumentation), spanning multiple components and teams. It is not documentation-only.\n20\t\n21\tAll components referenced by the strategy (Dashboard, Notebooks, Data Science\n22\tPipelines) have architecture-context files in `.context/architecture-context/`\n23\t(rhoai-3.0), so no onboarding chains or provisioning investigations are required.\n24\tNotebooks and Data Science Pipelines are **passive** components in this strategy:\n25\tthe launch mechanics use their existing, documented interfaces (Notebook CRD via\n26\tthe Dashboard; KFP v2 pipeline import), so no code changes are needed in them.\n27\tTheir validation is folded in as acceptance criteria on the gallery launch epic\n28\tand the tutorial testing epics; because the validating teams (Workbenches, RHOAI\n29\tPipelines) own the tutorial content epics that exercise those paths, no separate\n30\tvalidation epics are generated.\n31\t\n32\t## Epic List\n33\t\n34\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n35\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n36\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E001 | Tutorial packaging format and validation manifest | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P0 |