idated per the same format. |\n64\t| E002 ∥ E003, E002 ∥ E004 | Rule 14 (different repos, no shared artifacts) | Gallery code and tutorial content live in different repos owned by different teams. The end-to-end coupling is expressed as an AC on the gallery epic (launch verified with a tutorial packaged in the format), not as a DAG edge — the gallery can be developed and reviewed against a draft tutorial while the curated set is authored. |\n65\t| E003 ∥ E004 | Rule 1 / Rule 14 | Different components and teams (Notebooks/Workbenches vs Data Science Pipelines/RHOAI Pipelines); no shared artifacts beyond the common format both already depend on. |\n66\t| E001, E002, E003, E004 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs last) | The documentation describes the gallery, the tutorial set, and the contribution process as built, so it is blocked by every Implementation epic in the strategy. |\n67\t\n68\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n69\t\n70\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) | Notes |\n71\t|-----|----------|---------|-------|\n72\t| HLR-1 (tutorial gallery with one-click launch) | P0 | E002 | Direct mapping. |\n73\t| HLR-2 (six curated, tested tutorials) | P0 | E003, E004 | Split along the component/team boundary: five notebook-based journeys (first workbench, data prep, first training run, first deployment, first RAG app) in E003; the pipeline-based journey (first pipeline) in E004. Both cover HLR-2 together; neither alone satisfies it. |\n74\t| HLR-3 (tutorial packaging format) | P1 | E001 | Epic raised to P0 by priority inheritance: the format gates all P0 delivery (HLR-1 and HLR-2 both build against it), so the prerequisite inherits the highest priority it transitively enables. See Health Warnings. |\n75\t| HLR-4 (gallery and contribution documentation) | P2 | E005 | `docs-authoring` priority exception: derived from strategy frontmatter `priority: Major` → P1. |\n76\t\n77\tAll four HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n78\t\n79\t## Health Warnings\n80\t\n81\t- **Missing strategy sections (non-blocking):** the strategy has no Impacted Teams\n82\t  table, no Dependencies table, no formal Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, and\n83\t  no non-functional requirements section. Teams were inferred from the\n84\t  architecture-context owning teams (Dashboard → RHOAI Dashboard, Notebooks →\n85\t  Workbenches, Data Science Pipelines → RHOAI Pipelines; the Documentation team\n86\t  has no context file and was assigned by convention). Acceptance criteria below\n87\t  were derived from the HLRs.\n88\t- **Priority inheritance, not inversion:** HLR-3 is labeled P1, but its epic (E001)\n89\t  is P0 because every P0 deliverable (gallery and tutorials) builds against the\n90\t  format. This is standard prerequisite priority inheritance, flagged here for\n91\t  reviewer visibility.\n92\t- **Scope trap — RAG journey (architecture claim uncorroborated):** HLR-2 includes\n93\t  a \"first RAG app\" tutorial, but no architecture-context file covers a RAG\n94\t  capability in the platform (no context file exists for Llama Stack or any other\n95\t  RAG-bearing component). The tutorial epic is unaffected — it is authored either\n96\t  way — but if no supported RAG surface exists at release time, that one tutorial\n97\t  may need to build the RAG app from generic workbench/serving primitives or be\n98\t  descoped. Verify during epic refinement; this does not change the epic DAG.\n99\t- **Component mapping note (E001):** the packaging format is consumed by the\n100\t  Dashboard gallery implementation and by both tutorial-content epics, so its work\n101\t  spans several strategy components. It is assigned the single canonical component\n102\t  `Dashboard` as the most-relevant consumer (the gallery parses the metadata and\n103\t  launch mechanics use the pinned images), owned by RHOAI Dashboard.\n104\t- **Epic-size watch item (E003):** E003 bundles five curated, tested tutorials\n105\t  (authoring + packaging + release testing) and sits at the upper bound of the\n106\t  ~2-week guideline. It is kept as one epic because it is a single logical\n107\t  work stream (same component/team tuple, same packaging format, same testing\n108\t  pass) — a split would duplicate the testing/setup overhead and fragment the\n109\t  journey set. Re-split trigger: if authoring and validating the five\n110\t  tutorials outgrows a single sprint of effort, split E003 along journey\n111\t  lines — first-workbench/data-prep/first-training vs\n112\t  first-deployment/first-RAG-app — into two epics under the same team, with\n113\t  both depending on the packaging-format epic and both blocking the\n114\t  documentation epic (no other DAG edges change).\n115\t- **Tutorial-type assumption:** the strategy does not state which of the six\n116\t  tutorials are notebooks and which are pipelines. This decomposition assumes five\n117\t  notebook-based and one pipeline-based tutorial. If refinement assigns more\n118\t  journeys to pipelines, move them into the pipeline tutorial epic — a content\n119\t  reassignment within the same DAG, no structural change.\n120\t\n121\tNo epic exceeds the ~2-week epic-size guideline outright; E003 is at the upper\n122\tbound and carries a re-split trigger in Health Warnings. The six tutorials are\n123\tsplit across two teams and the gallery is one Dashboard feature.\n124\t\n125\t## Tiered Delivery\n126\t\n127\tNot applicable. The strategy has no external dependencies with uncertain timing\n128\t(no upstream contributions, vendor coordination, or third-party gating); all work\n129\tis in-platform and ships together.\n130\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2c680267fccf75d","agent_id":"a3400be638653be5c","session_id":"7d9fc257-6641-4b77-aebe-6dc2ab6f744b","uuid":"6d96d7f4-9092-4c94-b81b-0106682ce1f4","timestamp":"2026-10-25T19:19:30.335Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-87931a482bffa201","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Final